#!/bin/sh
# Builds the release programs for every platform into a directory, with a
# checksums.txt beside them. The builds are reproducible: with the Go release
# go.mod names, anyone gets the same bytes, so bin/checksums.txt can be
# checked against them.
#
#   scripts/build-release VERSION DIR
set -eu

version=$1 out=$2
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."
export GOTOOLCHAIN="go$(go list -m -f '{{.GoVersion}}')" CGO_ENABLED=0

mkdir -p "$out"
for target in darwin/amd64 darwin/arm64 linux/amd64 linux/arm64 windows/amd64 windows/arm64; do
	os=${target%/*} arch=${target#*/} ext=
	[ "$os" = windows ] && ext=.exe
	GOOS=$os GOARCH=$arch go build -trimpath -buildvcs=false -ldflags='-s -w -buildid=' \
		-o "$out/codex-micro-$version-$os-$arch$ext" ./cmd/codex-micro
done
(cd "$out" && sha256sum codex-micro-* > checksums.txt)
